yamlover/pointer
description: A * dereference over an unquoted colon path with the scope ladder
- >
  A **pointer** is `*` followed by an UNQUOTED colon path — the value IS the node the path
  names, a shared edge rather than a copy. More colons at the start widen the scope — bare is
  the current mapping (a sibling), `:` the document root, `::` the project, `:::` the world. A
  bare integer portion is a POSITION, `: name` a string key, `: '1'` the numeric STRING key:
- !!<format: text/x-yamlover> |
  feline: *pets: 1
  topDog: *: pets: 0
  secondName: *pets: 1: name
- >
  YAML's `*alias` maps to the document-scope `*: name` — the YAML alias is the subclass, and
  where the alias can only name a whole anchored node, the pointer path reaches INTO anything:
- *..:..:..:..:..:04-yaml:01-yaml_code:01-yaml_scalar:04-yaml_alias
